{
    "about": "Cases of the check of the original on the main site (documentation/Canonical Form.md, section \"The original of a note\", PUB-100, IDX-11 to IDX-13). The TypeScript and the Rust implementation both read this file. `noteTypes`: the note types whose notes also exist on the main site. `forms`: a text and its comparison form (`null`: not a URL that the check reads). `ghostProperty`: the property that the Ghost Publish plugin writes into every note that it posted. `properties`: a note with its note type (`null`: none), whether it also exists on the main site (`inScope`), and its post URL (`null`: none). `canonicals`: the head of a page, the URL of the page, and the canonical links that it names, resolved. `entries`: the key `original` of a manifest entry, as JSON text (`null`: no such key), and whether the entry is read. `judged`: the post URL of a note, the answer of the main site (or the failure of the request), and whether the post is verified. Each expected result is written by hand.",
